  "problem": "Which of the following values \u200bare possible outputs of $f(x)=-{(2)}^{-x}?$\n\n- $0$\n- $0.5$\n- $-0.5$",
  "worked_solution": "The range of ${2}^{-x}$ is\n\n$$\n{2}^{-x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1){(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ -{(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ f(x) & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<0.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-0.5$ is an output of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/95ad3043259402375e7b5822aef88d77027222a3372c2b8ab042d1b54e08666f.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
